{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "Kofra API",
    "version": "1.0.0-alpha.1",
    "summary": "Manage a Kofra storage workspace programmatically.",
    "description": "The Kofra API manages a storage workspace: buckets, S3 access keys, usage,\nthe account's state and its event feed. Object data is never sent to this\nAPI; read and write objects through the S3 endpoint with any S3 tool, or\nwith a presigned URL from `POST /v1/objects/presign`.\n\n**Status: draft.** This contract is published ahead of the service. The\nmock server in the repository answers every operation with the examples\nbelow.\n\nConventions:\n\n- Authentication: `Authorization: Bearer <API token>`. A token belongs to\n  exactly one workspace, so paths carry no workspace ID.\n- Errors: RFC 9457 `application/problem+json` with a stable `code`, a\n  one-sentence `hint` and a `docs_url`. See the error catalogue.\n- Lists: cursor pagination with `limit` (1 to 200, default 50) and\n  `cursor`; the body has `data` and `next_cursor` (`null` at the end), and\n  a `Link: <...>; rel=\"next\"` header repeats it.\n- Writes: `POST`, `PATCH` and `DELETE` accept `Idempotency-Key`, kept 24\n  hours and bound to the method, path, query and body of its first\n  request. Destructive operations accept `dry_run=true`.\n- Every response carries `Kofra-Request-Id`, `RateLimit` and\n  `RateLimit-Policy`; `429` and `503` also carry `Retry-After`, and `401`\n  carries `WWW-Authenticate`.\n- Unknown request fields and undeclared or repeated query parameters are\n  refused (`unknown_field`, `validation_failed`). Clients must ignore\n  unknown response fields, and treat an unknown enum value in a response\n  as \"other\": new fields and new enum values are added within `/v1`.\n- Timestamps are RFC 3339 UTC. Sizes are integers in bytes, in fields that\n  end in `_bytes`.\n",
    "license": {
      "name": "MIT",
      "identifier": "MIT"
    },
    "contact": {
      "name": "Kofra API",
      "url": "https://kofra.app/docs/api"
    }
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "https://api.kofra.app",
      "description": "Production (not live yet)"
    }
  ],
  "tags": [
    {
      "name": "Account",
      "description": "The workspace's state, limits and deletion."
    },
    {
      "name": "Buckets",
      "description": "Create, list and delete buckets. Objects are managed through S3."
    },
    {
      "name": "Access keys",
      "description": "S3 access key pairs and their per-bucket grants."
    },
    {
      "name": "Usage",
      "description": "Stored bytes, uploads, downloads and the daily series."
    },
    {
      "name": "Events",
      "description": "The workspace's event feed."
    },
    {
      "name": "Objects",
      "description": "Presigned URLs for the S3 endpoint."
    }
  ],
  "externalDocs": {
    "description": "Kofra API documentation",
